  "answer": "Petrol prices are about **13.5% higher than a year ago**. In August 2026 the automotive fuel index was 112.95, up from 99.49 in August 2025.\n\nThe increase has been bumpy. Fuel prices jumped 24.2% in March 2026 and 18.6% in April, fell back to a low in June, and then rose 13.5% in August. The latest figure is August 2026, the most recent monthly CPI release available to me.\n\nThe CPI measures a basket of automotive fuels nationally, not pump prices in cents per litre, so I can't give you an exact per-litre figure. If you tell me what you usually pay per litre, I can estimate what 13.5% means in dollars.",
